{"id": "section-body-13454", "title": "Oculocutaneous albinism", "chapterId": "chapter-thirteen", "tocLevel": 4, "tocPath": ["APPROACH TO PATIENTS WITH EMERGENCY CONDITIONS", "SKIN DISEASES", "Pigmentary Disorders", "Oculocutaneous albinism"], "blocks": [{"id": "body-13454", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Oculocutaneous albinism", "runs": [{"text": "Oculocutaneous"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "albinism"}], "level": 4, "list": {"level": 2, "numberingId": "1368"}}, {"id": "body-13455", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Oculocutaneous albinism (OCA) is a genetic disorder characterized by the complete or partial absence of melanin pigment in the skin, hair, and eyes. Reduced skin pigmentation leads to photosensitivity and increased skin cancer risk.", "runs": [{"text": "Oculocutaneous albinism (OCA) is a genetic disorder characterized by the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "complete or partial absence of melanin pigment in the skin, hair, and eyes. Reduced skin pigmentation leads to photosensitivity and increased skin cancer risk."}]}, {"id": "body-13458", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Clinical Presentation:", "runs": [{"text": "Clinical"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Presentation:"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-13459", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Ocular findings: Photophobia, reduced visual acuity, strabismus, nystagmus, and lack of binocular vision.", "runs": [{"text": "Ocular findings: Photophobia, reduced visual acuity, strabismus, nystagmus, and lack of binocular vision."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1322"}}, {"id": "body-13461", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Complete or partial absence of pigmentation on the skin, hair and eyes", "runs": [{"text": "Complete or partial absence of pigmentation on the skin, hair and eyes"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1322"}}, {"id": "body-13465", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Non-Pharmacological Ma